ount * 100)`, which cuts off the decimals instead of rounding. Float arithmetic leaves values just under the whole cent, so they lost a cent: `19.99 * 100` came out as 1998, and `0.29 * 100 = 28.999\u2026` came out as 28. With `qty=3` that gave 84 instead of 87, and the discount test was off for the same reason.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now returns `round(amount * 100)`. That rounds to the nearest cent and returns an int. Prices with two decimals can never land exactly on half a cent, so Python's round-half-to-even behaviour doesn't come into play.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 6, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 60471, "requests_cache_write": 128156, "requests_cost_usd": 0.6803301999999999, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1370, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 185, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T02:25:28.855689+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 26.18, "t_checker_s": 0.323, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1384, "tokens_cache_read": 60471, "tokens_cache_write": 128156, "tokens_fresh": 1384, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 60471, "tokens_main_cache_write": 128156, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_output": 1370, "tokens_output": 1370, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 60471, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 128156, "tokens_proxy_calls": 6, 